# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Derived rasters. `scans/` is exactly `pdftoppm -r <dpi>` over `pdfs/` —
# verified pixel-identical — so it is regenerable, not source. Keeping it out
# matters: it is 212 MB at 150 dpi and grows with every re-render, and git
# would keep each generation forever.
scans/

# Downloaded model weights (675 MB), not authored here.
models/

# Transient working dirs: recognition output kept only for comparison, and
# the sxiv review gates.
ocr300/
figs-ocr300/

# `review/` is mostly derived — line crops and generated HTML, regenerable from
# the ALTO and the rasters. But `review/proposals/` and `review/decisions/` are
# authored: a reading proposal is somebody's (or something's) transcription of a
# page, and an adjudication is an editorial act. Losing either is the failure this
# repo already suffered once. Note `review/*` rather than `review/`, because git
# will not descend into an excluded directory and the negations below would never
# be consulted.
review/*
!review/proposals/
!review/decisions/
# The save writes temp-then-rename and keeps one .prev alongside, as insurance
# against an interrupted write. Neither belongs in history — git is the history.
review/decisions/*.prev
review/decisions/*.tmp

# Symlink farms pointing *into* `scans/`, which is ignored above — so committing
# them yields 272 dangling links on a fresh clone. Regenerable from the `fig/` and
# `ocr/` listings, i.e. derived by the same argument that keeps `scans/` out.
# `ocr/` is deliberately NOT here: its symlinks resolve inside the repo, into
# `gt/ocr/`.
scans-w-figs/
scans-w-ocr/
